      "text_sha256": "ad374f418fddf38bb4707139a0f574123e657db813954a36f7f569d494c1e39e",
      "text": "Please note that all accounts take up four columns; two columns for the debit side and two columns for the credit side. Use the light grey column on each side for the reference to the contra entry. Use the white cells on each side for the recorded amounts. Also, use square brackets for the contra entry reference to avoid Excel transforming the information into a negative value. The cell references can either be written in, or selected using the droplist. No other information than the references can be added here. See example below:",
      "evidence_id": "instructions_A3"
    },
    {
      "sheet": "Instructions",
      "range": "A21:H24",
      "text_sha256": "ebed204192bd69decab5e0725b7ed51c7b03e9204a26e139d6c97717bf67b674",
      "text": "Please  note that this spreadsheet is not locked.  Try not to change the structure of the Excel sheet. Don't forget to add your information on the assigned space!",
      "evidence_id": "instructions_A21"
    }
  ],
